 "tab_about": "Contract v1.24 §24.1 (the core's tab rules) on top of the §12.4/§12.4a rules of `cases`. Extra fields: conversation = 'grp' | 'dm'; tab = the base epoch's group_meta.tab ('private' also for dm:); agents = the base epoch's group_meta.agents; agent_users = the users whose leaf attestation says kind: 'agent' (a leaf of such a user is an agent leaf); meta may also carry tab (the new value, or null if unchanged), chat_id_changed and agents (the new list, or null if unchanged). Rules: tab and chat_id never change after epoch 0; a dm: or Private group has agents == [] and never gains an agent leaf; in Official an agent leaf may be added only by an admin and only for a user in agents (base or new), agents never names an admin; any member may remove every leaf of an agent (never a part of them) in a commit that otherwise touches only the committer's own leaves and changes no group_meta. Every other commit follows the rules of `cases`. The `cases` above carry no tab: they are Official groups (they list an agent) and keep their expectations under v1.24. v1.25 (§25.2): a case may also carry chat_kind ('risi' for a user's Risi chat: an Official group whose chat_id is its own conversation id, chat_id_is_own = true). Runners that don't know these fields ignore them: a Risi chat follows the Official rules, so the Risi-chat cases here are accepted by the v1.24 rules too. The extra Risi-chat rules are in `risi_cases`.",
