 "risi_about": "Contract v1.25 §25.2 (crypto C4): the core's extra rules for a Risi chat, on top of `tab_cases`. Fields as in tab_cases; chat_kind = the base epoch's group_meta.chat_kind ('risi'); chat_id_is_own = the base epoch's chat_id equals the group's own conversation id; meta may also carry chat_kind_changed. Rules: a group_meta with chat_kind 'risi' has tab 'official', chat_id equal to its own conversation id, exactly one human user (its only admin) and agents == [the agent]; chat_kind never changes after epoch 0 (absent counts as not 'risi'); no commit adds a leaf of a second human user. Everything else follows `tab_cases` and `cases`. Run by the core once C4 lands (the v1.24 runners don't read this list; the 'second human' and 'chat_kind change' cases would pass the v1.24 rules).",
